A||||2||84Bill||Gauge faces shortcut||||3||
Z||000000||84Bill||06-16-2001||02:25 PM||||I was noticing all the whoopla about gauge faces lately. <BR>Well last week I finaly found a Full instrument cluster with a tach and gauges for my 93 Corsica. I put it in and had the other one sitting here for a few days and decided to examine it a bit closer and lookie what I found out.<P>here is the old instrument cluster, the speedo face is roughly the same size as the Fieros<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://cn308598-a.wall1.pa.home.com/gages/image002.jpg">   <P>As you can see it is backlit in blue.   <IMG SRC="http://cn308598-a.wall1.pa.home.com/gages/image004.jpg">  <P>Here you can see how the needles get lit from the plastic backing.<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://cn308598-a.wall1.pa.home.com/gages/image006.jpg">   <P>And best of all is you can PEEL THE FACE RIGHT OFF! I can't imagine it being to hard using compass to scribe a circle around the speedo and cut it out.<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://cn308598-a.wall1.pa.home.com/gages/image008.jpg">    <P>FYI the Baretta's also have the same cluster and some have the FULL instrument package. It cost me 30 bucks at a salvage yard for the full cluster with tach , volt meter, oil pressure and temp gauges built in it. I think with a little care you can even cut out the idiot light film and transplant it to the Fieros idiot lights.<P><p>[This message has been edited by 84Bill (edited 06-16-2001).]||||reg||3
Z||000001||FieroJoe||06-16-2001||10:34 PM||||Speaking of idiot lights...<P>I have been lately working on having a Pegasus light up instead of the shift light.  I was thinking of making my own brand new set of overlays, and maybe even doing them in white, like 88CoupeV6's, to match my white gauges.  But, I didnt think that I could make them as nice as his, so I just printed out a outline of the pegasus, used some acetone to remove the old "shift" lettering, and stuck it there.  I haven't installed it yet, but I'm planning on it soon.<P>88CoupeV6 - if you read this, and if you have time, I'd like for you to make me a set of those warning light overlays, and possibly have something different for the shift light, like a pegasus or something different even.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
Z||000002||AusFiero||06-17-2001||06:12 AM||||Interesting idea Bill. Particularly with so many gauge panels already lieing around junkyards. You will find most are stick on. Well GM ones anyway.||||reg||14
